"Court" means any court in Guyana having jurisdiction to hear and determine causes and matters, whether civil or criminal;
"facts in issue" means -
(a) all facts which, by the form of the pleadings in any action or other proceeding, are affirmed on one side and denied on other; and
(b) in actions or other proceedings in which there are no pleadings, or in which the form of the pleadings is such that distinct issues are not joined between the parties, all facts from the establishment of which the existence, non-existence, nature, or extent of any right, liability, or disability, asserted, or denied, in any such case would by law follow;
